missingTests.body:
The new unit tests cover the validator in isolation, which is the right start, but every failure found in review lives outside that boundary:

- no test drives a controller against an **existing** deprecated-type group, which is how the three-writer problem went unnoticed;
- no test **renders the chart**, which is how the default-value mismatch and the value-shape failures went unnoticed;
- no test **converts a v1alpha1 object and then validates the result**, which is the whole v1alpha1 chain.

Each is a few lines and each would have caught a blocking issue.
